{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01J9HDWkYPAnvYYyN6r5kSvj","type":"tool_result","content":"== batch\n  mutation: creates declared Task-Spec scaffolds; --dry-run writes nothing\n  usage: Usage: taskspec batch --plan <TaskPlan.yaml> | taskspec batch --intent-file <file> --effort <size>\n  summary: creates declared Task-Spec scaffolds; --dry-run writes nothing\n== gate\n  mutation: executes task evals; --stamp additionally writes the sign-off envelope\n  usage: Usage: taskspec gate [--stamp] [--require-tier1] <task-spec>\n  summary: executes task evals; --stamp additionally writes the sign-off envelope\n== run\n  mutation: runs declared eval commands in the task workspace\n  usage: Usage: taskspec run [--ci] <task-spec>\n  summary: runs declared eval commands in the task workspace\n== accept\n  mutation: executes acceptance evals; --stamp additionally writes AcceptanceRecord/v1 and the acceptance envelope\n  usage: Usage: taskspec accept [--stamp] [--handoff <file>] [receipt flags] <task-spec>\n  summary: executes acceptance evals; --stamp additionally writes AcceptanceRecord/v1 and the acceptance envelope\n== mesh\n  mutation: optional repository-local control plane; run/cancel/resume/accept/finish/setup mutate disposable mesh state while canonical acceptance still calls Task-Spec\n  usage: Usage: taskspec mesh <init|doctor|serve|frontier|run|status|watch|explain|cancel|resume|accept|finish|adapters|setup|mcp> ... | taskspec mesh run --initiative <id> [--execute]\n  summary: optional repository-local control plane; run/cancel/resume/accept/finish/setup mutate disposable mesh state while canonical acceptance still calls Task-Spec\n== graph\n  mutation: none; TaskGraphView/v1 is derived from Markdown and Git\n  usage: Usage: taskspec graph [--task <id>] [--check] [--mermaid] [--json] | taskspec graph --initiative <id> --view tasks|capabilities\n  summary: none; TaskGraphView/v1 is derived from Markdown and Git\n== status\n  mutation: none; emits TaskStatus/v1 and exactly one safe next command\n  usage: Usage: taskspec status <task-id-or-path> [--json] | taskspec status --initiative <id>\n  summary: none; emits TaskStatus/v1 and exactly one safe next command\n== decompose status\n  mutation: none\n  usage: Usage: taskspec decompose status <initiative>\n  summary: Explain planning blockers and next valid action.\n== mesh init\n  mutation: mutates TaskMesh state; never grants a TaskSpec seal\n  usage: Usage: taskspec mesh init \n  summary: Use the existing TaskMesh init operation.\n== mesh doctor\n  mutation: may initialize a missing daemon and write Git metadata; does not seal or accept tasks\n  usage: Usage: taskspec mesh doctor \n  summary: Use the existing TaskMesh doctor operation.\n== mesh serve\n  mutation: mutates TaskMesh state; never grants a TaskSpec seal\n  usage: Usage: taskspec mesh serve --foreground\n  summary: Use the existing TaskMesh serve operation.\n== mesh frontier\n  mutation: may initialize a missing daemon and write Git metadata; does not seal or accept tasks\n  usage: Usage: taskspec mesh frontier \n  summary: Use the existing TaskMesh frontier operation.\n== mesh run\n  mutation: mutates TaskMesh state; never grants a TaskSpec seal\n  usage: Usage: taskspec mesh run --task <id>|--frontier|--initiative <id> [--adapter <name>] [--model <id>] [--provider <id>] [--mode supervised|autonomous] [--max-parallel <n>] [--execute]\n  summary: Creates a run, worktree and lease; --execute starts the executor; --dry-run previews without creating them.\n== mesh status\n  mutation: uninitialized status is read-only; existing runtime inspection may restart its daemon\n  usage: Usage: taskspec mesh status [<run-or-attempt>]\n  summary: Use the existing TaskMesh status operation.\n== mesh watch\n  mutation: may initialize a missing daemon and write Git metadata; does not seal or accept tasks\n  usage: Usage: taskspec mesh watch <run> [--after <sequence>]\n  summary: Use the existing TaskMesh watch operation.\n== mesh explain\n  mutation: may initialize a missing daemon and write Git metadata; does not seal or accept tasks\n  usage: Usage: taskspec mesh explain --task <id> [--adapter <name>] [--model <id>]\n  summary: Use the existing TaskMesh explain operation.\n== mesh cancel\n  mutation: mutates TaskMesh state; never grants a TaskSpec seal\n  usage: Usage: taskspec mesh cancel <attempt>\n  summary: Use the existing TaskMesh cancel operation.\n== mesh resume\n  mutation: mutates TaskMesh state; never grants a TaskSpec seal\n  usage: Usage: taskspec mesh resume <run-or-attempt> [--execute]\n  summary: Use the existing TaskMesh resume operation.\n== mesh accept\n  mutation: mutates TaskMesh state; never grants a TaskSpec seal\n  usage: Usage: taskspec mesh accept <attempt> --supervised-by <identity> --reason <text>\n  summary: Use the existing TaskMesh accept operation.\n== mesh finish\n  mutation: mutates TaskMesh state; never grants a TaskSpec seal\n  usage: Usage: taskspec mesh finish <run>\n  summary: Use the existing TaskMesh finish operation.\n== mesh adapters\n  mutation: may initialize a missing daemon and write Git metadata; does not seal or accept tasks; probe invokes adapter executables\n  usage: Usage: taskspec mesh adapters list|probe [<name>]\n  summary: Use the existing TaskMesh adapters operation.\n== mesh setup\n  mutation: mutates TaskMesh state; never grants a TaskSpec seal\n  usage: Usage: taskspec mesh setup sandbox\n  summary: Use the existing TaskMesh setup operation.\n== mesh mcp\n  mutation: none\n  usage: Usage: taskspec mesh mcp \n  summary: Use the existing TaskMesh mcp operation.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ec2e446b-ed72-415e-9175-fca87be396aa","uuid":"b5fe62b2-9605-43f7-9de6-f9727b871a8e","timestamp":"2026-09-15T11:19:57.858Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"== batch\n  mutation: creates declared Task-Spec scaffolds; --dry-run writes nothing\n  usage: Usage: taskspec batch --plan <TaskPlan